Replaces the custom purple/peach/mint palette with the Dracula color scheme (light + dark variants) and swaps the text pill toggle for a crescent moon / sun SVG icon button.

## Color tokens (`global.css`)
- `:root` — Dracula Light: `#f8f8f2` bg, `#282a36`/`#44475a` text, `#6d5b9c` primary (darkened for light-bg contrast), gradient `#bd93f9 → #ff79c6 → #8be9fd`
- `[data-theme="dark"]` — Dracula Dark: `#282a36` bg, `#44475a` surfaces, `#bd93f9` primary, `#ff79c6` pink accent
- All hardcoded hex values (blockquote, date badge) replaced with CSS variables

## Theme toggle (`Base.astro`)
- Button now contains inline moon + sun SVGs; visibility driven by CSS `[data-theme]` selectors — no JS DOM update needed
- JS toggle script simplified to just flip the attribute and persist to `localStorage`

```css
/* Icon visibility — purely CSS, no JS required */
.theme-toggle .icon-sun { display: none; }
.theme-toggle .icon-moon { display: block; }

html[data-theme="dark"] .theme-toggle .icon-sun { display: block; }
html[data-theme="dark"] .theme-toggle .icon-moon { display: none; }
```

Fixes a type error with trigger's that redeclare their ref as HTMLElement, repro:
```tsx
const triggerRef = React.useRef<HTMLElement>(null);
 // Type 'RefObject<HTMLElement | null>' is not assignable to type '((((instance: HTMLButtonElement | null) => void |…
<Popover.Trigger ref={triggerRef} />;
```

